      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i feel like the 'religious liberal' side sounds a lot more philosophically grounded in the way you described it, focusing on stuff like autonomy and dignity. but when you talk about the conservative side, it sounds almost like they're just saying 'because the book says so.' can you go deeper into the actual ethical frameworks conservatives use? like, what's the logical basis for the 'sanctity of life' argument beyond just quoting scripture?",
